ple to write with  chalk on the city's most famous building  sometimes graphic messages yes I'm  pretty direct messages for the police  department here and we're fine with that  because these messages can be removed in  the initial round of protests the city's  residents watched as one man threw a  burning object through a city hall  window  he was arrested the next day and Brown  says he'll be fully prosecuted so get  ready because we're coming all while  protesters gather not just outside the  mayor's place of work but his home  you've got white protesters holding  black lives matter signs outside your  house when you see that what's your  reaction I am glad that people finally  realize after 400 years in this country  that black lives matter why did it take  the death of George Floyd to have some  of these conversations it was a  flashpoint it was just a continuation of  things that we've seen in this country  before Eric garner of Brianna Taylor  Freddie gray Ahmad our burry and the  anger the frustration just bubbled over  they all have been painful they all have  been distressing this took on a life of  its own it's been played over and over  and over again when my family and I  first watched that together there were  tears in my house  I almost feel it now just thinking about  it I see that is this a process that  takes a lot longer than most people  think I think it is a process that will  take longer than most people think but  it's a process that has to be approached  with a listening ear with an open heart  and with great urgency
 

